   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amid the profound transformations in the Arab States region&#x2014;characterized by political, economic, and social instability&#x2014;the rapid implementation of structural adjustment programs further underscores the urgent need for a just transition. This approach is essential to ensuring fairness and inclusivity in addressing the impacts of economic, social, and environmental changes. Strong and representative workers&apos; organizations are pivotal in influencing policy decisions and safeguarding the rights and interests of all workers, particularly during these transitional periods.
Achieving certain outcomes such as just transition requires workers&apos; organizations to overcome significant challenges and strengthen their capacities through comprehensive technical, institutional, and evidence-based support. Priority areas include organizing, collective bargaining, outreach to informal workers, and robust policy analysis and formulation. These efforts are vital to empowering workers&apos; organizations to effectively advocate for workers&apos; aspirations and ensure their voices remain central to the process.
The ILO is steadfast in its commitment to supporting workers in realizing a just transition in the region focused on strengthening the role of Arab trade unions to better advocate for workers&#x2019; rights and secure fundamental protections, including freedom of association and collective bargaining. In collaboration with the Arab Trade Union Confederation (ATUC), the ILO aims to support affiliated organizations in assessing and revising the developed regional trade union strategy on just transition to ensure that workers&apos; organizations play a central role in shaping fair and inclusive policies to address the region&apos;s emerging challenges and opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
